            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for given that, then the Arabic for in order to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: مع ذلك",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مع ذلك — maʿa dhālika — \"even so; however\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "كان متعبا، مع ذلك أكمل عمله. kāna mutʿaban, maʿa dhālika akmala ʿamalah. He was tired; even so, he finished his work."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often with و: ومع ذلك, and yet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مع ذلك (maʿa dhālika) joins two native Arabic words, maʿa, \"with\", and dhālika, \"that\": with all that, even so. The deeper origin of such particles is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
