              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "علاوة على — ʿilāwatan ʿalā — \"moreover; on top of\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "علاوة على الراتب، يحصل الموظف على سيارة. ʿilāwatan ʿalā ar-rātib, yaḥṣulu al-muwaẓẓaf ʿalā sayyāra. On top of the salary, the employee gets a car."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also علاوة alone: a bonus on a salary."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "علاوة على (ʿilāwatan ʿalā) is built on the native Arabic root ʿ-l-w, \"to be high, to rise above\" (Lane). ʿIlāwa is what is laid on top of a load: something extra, and so moreover."
            }
          ]
        },
